From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 03:06:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: exp - NyaCore candidate C: NavigationSnapshot,
 SnapshotWalkNodeEvaluator, SnapshotEntityCollisionContext,
 NavigationPathfindPhase

Per DEC-70 3rd section steps 3-5. NavigationSnapshot is the immutable,
worker-safe capture of every live Mob read WalkNodeEvaluator's search needs
(field list traces 1:1 to evidence/20260806-nyacore-candidate-c-
navigationsnapshot-design.md 1a/1b/3c). SnapshotWalkNodeEvaluator overrides
every accessor patch 0150/0151 introduced to read the snapshot instead of a
live Mob - this.mob is never assigned, so a missed override fails loudly
(NPE) instead of silently reaching a live object.
SnapshotEntityCollisionContext replaces CollisionContext.of(mob)'s live
entity reference with two booleans captured on the owner thread (design doc
3d - the only real use was canStandOnFluid, and every known implementation
of that only depends on fluid type). NavigationPathfindPhase wires this into
the existing RegionParallelRunner/RegionParallelPhase framework unchanged -
snapshot()/compute()/commit() run on the threads the framework already
guarantees, reusing its bounded queue, deadline, and ownership/lifecycle
re-validation as-is. Scoped to ground navigation only for this first wiring
per DEC-70 (villager AI is the required first workload).

Real build+smoke-test cycle before this commit: compiled successfully
(BUILD SUCCESSFUL), deployed to lophinya-loadprobe, spawnfarm 100 villagers
still pathfind and claim POIs normally (employed=8/100, non-zero, no
exceptions) after the prerequisite WalkNodeEvaluator accessor refactor -
this commit adds the actual snapshot-mode classes on top of that already-
verified base.

Still not done: no real trigger wires NavigationPathfindPhase into an actual
villager AI call site yet (it is invocable but nothing calls it in normal
play), and none of DEC-70 6 benchmark matrix has been run against it.

